Description: Reimplements the assimilative causal inference (ACI) method of
    Andreou, Chen and Bollt (2026) <doi:10.1038/s41467-026-68568-0> for
    conditional Gaussian nonlinear systems (CGNS). Provides the closed-form
    forward filter and backward smoother for the conditional Gaussian
    statistics of an unobserved component given an observed signal, together
    with the relative-entropy causal-information metric that contrasts the
    smoother posterior against the filter posterior. The numerical core is
    graded against fixtures generated by an independent 'MATLAB' harness
    reproducing the deterministic core of the reference implementation. Also
    provides the fixed-lag online smoother and the causal influence range,
    which measures how far ahead in the observed record the estimate of the
    unobserved state keeps improving, and the noisy predator-prey model in
    either causal direction. Vector-valued states and the conditional
    construction are supported throughout, including the fixed-lag online
    smoother and the causal influence range built on it.
